=== abstract-level parity (S4: no digitized data exists) ===
  A2: NOT TESTED HERE. k_m = 0 above 70 C is an INPUT (slot S2 encodes
      the abstract's claim), so the 0.000000 % methanation loss at 90 C
      is that input read back, not a check of it. Testing A2 needs the
      paper's rate law (S2) with its own temperature dependence.
  M2 (a computed result): at 25 C the calcite net balance peaks INSIDE
      the A interval (5.383 mmol at A = 6e-6), above both corners
      (about 4.11 and 0.68 mmol): corner-only interval propagation would
      report a bound that excludes a reachable value. The scan catches it.
  A3: at 25-50 C the limited-H2 batch loses ~0.2-2.6 % over 30 yr
      (ILLUSTRATIVE k_m anchored to Bo 2021 field losses, P4) —
      the paper's 'considerable consumption' finding awaits its
      kinetic law (S2) for any quantitative comparison.
  A4: physical dissolution loss is not a sink in this network;
      the abstract's <1 % molar figure is about solubility
      trapping and is NOT claimed here.

  What a point-value PHREEQC run prints: one trajectory per T.
  What this file adds: the native GUM band (with its own engine
  caveats printed), the corner p-boxes through the integration,
  the monotonicity labels, and the slots where the paper's
  calibrated expressions drop in — 2-line edits, every number
